# lb/bench_runner/.env -- ONE deployment's sealed swarm runner (gitignored: copy this file to .env and
# fill in every line). Each deployment has its own box name, docker network, LB and engine, so nothing
# here has a default: compose refuses an unset value and names it. Values are plain KEY=VALUE, no quotes,
# no inline comments. A deploy/standalone server keeps no .env here: up.sh derives all five from its
# server file.

# The box this runner runs on, as the deployment names it: the gateway panel says "runner on <box>".
BENCH_BOX=

# The LB's swarm directory on THIS host: the directory the vllm-lb container mounts as its LB_SWARM_STATE
# (lb/docker-compose.yml mounts lb/state at /data, and LB_SWARM_STATE is /data/benchq), as an absolute path.
BENCH_STATE_DIR=

# The docker network where the egress container reaches BOTH targets below (the LB's network; on a server
# whose engine is a container, the network the LB and the engine share). It must exist already. With the
# broker on, the LB's only network is the broker's: give the LB its own with lb/docker-compose.bench-net.yml
# and name that network here — the same value as lb/.env's LB_BENCH_NETWORK.
BENCH_UPSTREAM_NETWORK=

# The LB's API, host:port, as seen from that network (the vllm-lb container listens on 8010). The runner itself
# calls http://lb:8010 through the egress relay, so the LB sees `Host: lb:8010`: list it in the LB's
# LB_ALLOWED_HOSTS (lb/.env), or every swarm turn is answered 421.
BENCH_LB_TARGET=

# The engine's own API, host:port, whose /metrics the session's guard C reads: the head rank's vLLM or
# SGLang port (the same host:port as the LB's LB_CLUSTER_URL), or the node container's on a single-GPU
# server. It must be a private address: the egress refuses a public one.
BENCH_ENGINE_TARGET=

# ── only on a host whose docker has no free address pool (compose: "fully subnetted") ─────────────
# Uncomment both: subnet.yml puts the sealed network on the subnet you name. Nothing picks one for you.
# COMPOSE_FILE=docker-compose.yml:subnet.yml
# BENCH_SEALED_SUBNET=
